# Oh My Pi state dir: tracked config only, runtime state never.
#
# ~/.omp is an out-of-store symlink to THIS directory, so omp writes all of
# its live state here (dbs, sessions, logs, caches, daemons). Only genuine
# config is committed; everything omp generates at runtime stays local.
#
# Pattern per gitignore semantics: ignore every entry under agent/, then
# re-include the tracked ones (a re-include can't resurrect files inside an
# ignored directory, so tracked subdirectories are negated as dirs first).

agent/*
!agent/RULES.md
!agent/managed-skills/
!agent/managed-skills/**
!agent/scripts/
!agent/scripts/**


# Declarative via home-manager (programs.omp.settings / ompMcp):
# config.yml and mcp.json are generated by `home.activation.ompConfig` /
# `ompMcp` from Nix (see modules/features/omp/default.nix) without secrets.
# They are ignored here (agent/* without ! re-include) so `home-manager
# switch` can overwrite the file inside the out-of-store ~/.omp symlink
# without dirtying the repo. To edit, change `programs.omp.settings` /
# mcpServers in default.nix, not the file in this checkout.


logs/
natives/
cache/
terminal-sessions/
puppeteer/
run/
ssh-control/

gpu_cache.json
install-id
autoqa.db
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
omp-session-*

plugins/node_modules/
